Lanelet2 stand-in for the NiFT web playground (nift_playground/py/fakelanelet2)

This package is part of the NiFT AV shuttle repository, which is Apache-2.0 licensed (see LICENSE at the repository
root). Several modules translate algorithms from third-party C++ libraries into Python. Those portions keep the
licences of their sources. The full licence texts are in LICENSES/ next to this file, and every module names its
sources in its docstring.

This is an independent reimplementation. It is not made, reviewed or endorsed by FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik, by
the Boost or GeographicLib authors, or by the owners of the Mcity Digital Twin. "Lanelet2" names the API this package
imitates. It does not mean the package comes from the Lanelet2 project.

Third-party portions, per file (paths relative to lanelet2/):

  __init__.py         no third-party code (package docstring only)

  core.py             Lanelet2 1.2.3: the Python API of lanelet2.core (class and method names, the semantics of
                      inverted primitives, Attribute::asBool / asDouble).
                      BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2018 FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik.
                      LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Lanelet2.txt

  _centerline.py      Lanelet2 1.2.3: calculateCenterline() and BoundChecker from lanelet2_core/src/Lanelet.cpp.
                      BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2018 FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik.
                      LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Lanelet2.txt

  geometry.py         Lanelet2 1.2.3: lanelet2_core geometry (LineStringGeometry, LaneletGeometry, findNearest from
                      LaneletMap.cpp, approximatedLength2d, toArcCoordinates, align / signedDistance).
                      BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2018 FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik.
                      LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Lanelet2.txt
                      Boost.Geometry 1.74: math::equals, compare::cartesian, side_by_triangle, the cartesian winding
                      point-in-ring test, projected-point distance and point-to-ring distance (_beq, _bless_pt,
                      _side_value, _side, _point_in_ring, _seg_cdist, _ring_distance).
                      BSL-1.0, see LICENSES/BSL-1.0-Boost.txt for the copyright holders of each header.

  _rtree.py           Boost.Geometry 1.74: the packing constructor of bgi::rtree with quadratic<16> and the
                      incremental nearest query (index/rtree.hpp, index/parameters.hpp,
                      index/detail/rtree/pack_create.hpp, index/detail/rtree/visitors/distance_query.hpp).
                      BSL-1.0, see LICENSES/BSL-1.0-Boost.txt.

  _utm.py             GeographicLib 1.52: TransverseMercator series and coefficient tables, Math helpers (sincosd,
                      atan2d, AngDiff, taupf, tauf), UTMUPS zone rules.
                      MIT, Copyright (c) 2008-2021, Charles Karney.
                      LICENSES/MIT-GeographicLib.txt
                      _hypot is Python's built-in math.hypot.

  projection.py       Lanelet2 1.2.3: UtmProjector from lanelet2_projection/src/UTM.cpp.
                      BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2018 FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik.
                      LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Lanelet2.txt

  io.py               Lanelet2 1.2.3: OsmFile.cpp and OsmHandlerLoad.cpp from lanelet2_io (load order, rules and
                      error messages).
                      BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2018 FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik.
                      LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Lanelet2.txt

  routing.py          Lanelet2 1.2.3: RoutingGraphBuilder.cpp, RoutingGraph.cpp and RoutingCost.h from
                      lanelet2_routing.
                      BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2018 FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik.
                      LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Lanelet2.txt

  traffic_rules.py    Lanelet2 1.2.3: GenericTrafficRules.cpp and GermanTrafficRules.cpp from lanelet2_traffic_rules.
                      BSD-3-Clause, Copyright 2018 FZI Forschungszentrum Informatik.
                      LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause-Lanelet2.txt

  _nodecache.py       no third-party code.

  node_cache/*.bin    Data, not code: map node coordinates computed by the real Lanelet2 from
                      maps/lanelet2_odr2024.osm, which is derived from the Mcity Digital Twin.
                      MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 Quantum Signal AI LLC, Copyright (c) 2024 The Regents of the University
                      of Michigan.
                      LICENSES/MIT-mcity-digital-twin.txt

  _rtree.py (sort_by_first, _coarse0, _WalkRecord), geometry.py (fast paths)
                      Our own code (Apache-2.0), added on top of the Boost-derived parts listed above.

  _stdorder.py        Our own code (Apache-2.0), no third-party portions. It reproduces the iteration order of a C++
                      hash map and the ordering of the C++ sort and select routines, written by an implementer who
                      only saw a behavioural specification (CLEANROOM_SPEC.md) and test vectors, never the C++
                      library sources.
